# ⛔ SNAPSHOTS AND CANDIDATE LISTS HOLD VERBATIM MEMO CONTENT, AND SOME MEMOS
# HOLD CREDENTIALS. `stage2-before/456582c0.json` captured the Omada admin
# password in plaintext before the audit redacted it from the corpus. Committing
# a snapshot would re-publish a secret into git history, where it is far harder
# to remove than from memo. [2026-10-19]
#
# These are also regenerable: `select-all.py` rebuilds the candidate lists and
# the snapshot step re-reads `GET /documents`. Nothing durable is lost.
candidates*.json
*-before/
runs/
